.TH ZCALLD 1 "November 2026" "zcalld" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zcalld \- compact Linux AI gateway with native plugins
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zcalld
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zcalld
serves a local HTTP gateway for AI clients. The zcall library handles model
protocols. System libcurl provides HTTP and TLS transport. Optional native
plugins are loaded through zplugin.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Run the gateway in the foreground. Under systemd, report readiness after startup.
.TP
.B check
Validate configuration without making an upstream model request.
.TP
.B models
Print configured model routes.
.TP
.B env
Print client environment settings. An optional argument selects
.BR openai ,
.BR anthropic ,
or
.BR gemini .
.TP
.B plugins
Inspect configured plugins.
.TP
.B init
Write an example configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-config " path
Use the specified configuration file. The default is
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/zcalld/config.conf
or
.BR $HOME/.config/zcalld/config.conf .
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print command help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/zcalld/config.conf
System service configuration. Package upgrades preserve local changes.
.TP
.B /etc/zcalld/credentials
Optional systemd environment file containing provider credentials.
.TP
.B ~/.config/zcalld/credentials
Optional user service environment file.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/zcalld/plugins/
Packaged optional native plugins. Installed plugins are loaded only when configured.
.SH SERVICE
Use one service scope for a given listening address and port.
.PP
.B systemctl --user enable --now zcalld.service
.PP
.B sudo systemctl enable --now zcalld.service
.PP
The system service uses a dynamic unprivileged account and reads configuration
from /etc/zcalld. The user service reads the user's default configuration path.
.SH SECURITY
Keep upstream keys in environment variables. Native plugins are trusted code
and execute with the service's privileges. Configure only trusted shared libraries.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.service (5)
